{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659621455988001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"courageous-deserving-manatee","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b476bc193b3881957032a38b53f0f707b91e5b1905f4da86607eda9a82a260b4","event_uuid":"993e9feb-c376-41cc-897c-08e9ec5926af","position":{"commit_sha":"934b9befbea810f182fd0e9a728c60cf4027281a","position":"1786597447143591001-993e9feb-c376-41cc-897c-08e9ec5926af"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bc3120a4d8754cb38bdd257e49cef41cfb73d798ea1436fa7433a50bdcc6887a","event_uuid":"054a4cb8-82b5-429f-9360-a4b88a5522c2","position":{"commit_sha":"3e31eba343d1af90ac2998cd0e9128aae6a3aa23","position":"1786597457702983001-054a4cb8-82b5-429f-9360-a4b88a5522c2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3242ad10f38a013e79b67fbed41ce28efb4701657b1e8f683fbd8dab1b3f06b6","event_uuid":"72126233-8423-4d8d-97f8-275672c97d75","position":{"commit_sha":"a094c0881b8a19fa6aeb1946a2db41bee3ed712d","position":"1786597476234053001-72126233-8423-4d8d-97f8-275672c97d75"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786597447143591001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"72126233-8423-4d8d-97f8-275672c97d75","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9efe-8e88-70b3-4984"}],"description":"## Context\nDiscovered while landing abasic-doddering-harrier (annotate the attest package for the typing ratchet). Annotating 12 `repo_root` parameters pushed four function signatures past the line-length limit, so `ruff format` wrapped them onto multiple lines. `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` went from **784 to 793 LOC** against the hard 800 cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n\nThe harrier change itself PASSES the module-size gate (793 < 800) and is correct as landed — this ticket is NOT a defect in it. But the file now has **7 lines of headroom**, which is effectively zero: the next routine edit (one new helper, one more wrapped signature, one added docstring line) trips the CI module-size gate and blocks an unrelated change with a failure that has nothing to do with its author's work.\n\nThis is the same near-cap class of finding the parent epic (broke-boarish-hagfish) is already draining for structured_run.py, compact.py, and event_append.py — authorship.py simply was not in the audit's near-cap set when the epic was scoped, because at 784 it sat just under the threshold and the typing work is what consumed the remaining margin.\n\n## Why a split rather than re-wrapping\nReverting the wrapping is not available: the wrapping is `ruff format` output and `make lint` runs `ruff format --check`, so the formatter's layout is the enforced one. The headroom has to come from removing code, not from reflowing it.\n\n## Plan\n- Split `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` along an EXISTING call-graph seam, per the AGENTS.md module-size policy (split only at seams that already exist; never mechanically to hit a number; never create a file < 100 LOC).\n- The obvious seam is the **git-ancestry/commit-resolution layer** — a cluster that already calls only into itself and `subprocess`, and is consumed by the verify layer through a narrow interface: `resolve_event_commit`, `resolve_position_commit`, `build_ticket_position_commit_map`, `build_introducing_commit_map`, `build_position_commit_map` (~330 LOC together, comfortably over the 100 LOC floor). The verification layer (`verify_authorship*`, `identify_signer`, `keys_valid_at_anchor`) stays put.\n- **Preserve public import paths** by re-exporting the moved symbols from `authorship`, so the split is behavior-identical. This matters more than usual here: tests reference these as `authorship.resolve_event_commit` (tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py, test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py, test_authorship_resolver_git_flags.py, test_identity_perf_1cc0.py) and at least one monkeypatches through that attribute, so the module attribute must keep resolving.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` reports a value that leaves real headroom under the 800 cap (target <= 500 per the AGENTS.md 200-500 target band).\n- [ ] Every new module created by the split is >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] Public import paths preserved: `python -c 'from rebar.attest import authorship; [getattr(authorship, n) for n in (\"resolve_event_commit\",\"resolve_position_commit\",\"build_ticket_position_commit_map\",\"build_introducing_commit_map\",\"build_position_commit_map\")]'` exits 0.\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` still reports no errors (the harrier invariant is not regressed by the split), and the Any-count grep over `src/rebar/attest/*.py` still reports exactly 2.\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and the CI pytest lane are green; no behavior change (annotations/imports only — no logic edits).\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` plus new sibling module(s) in the same package. Must land AFTER abasic-doddering-harrier (which is what creates the 793-line state).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","reason":"split near-cap module along the git-ancestry/commit-resolution call-graph seam"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"760f-608f-4c69-449a","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split authorship.py: 793/800 LOC, 7 lines of module-size headroom","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["993e9feb-c376-41cc-897c-08e9ec5926af","054a4cb8-82b5-429f-9360-a4b88a5522c2","72126233-8423-4d8d-97f8-275672c97d75"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659621455988001,"uuid":"27d76644-de04-4ba9-8ef4-a268a72511d2"}